  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Rhoda Chase has helped bring private art collections into public view. She and her daughter, Cheryl, shared their holdings through exhibitions at the New Britain Museum of American Art. Rhoda and her husband, David, were among the leading private donors to the campaign for the museum’s Chase Family Building. The expansion provided larger galleries while the older Landers House accommodated educational activities, a library and a studio.\n\nEducation has been another lasting commitment. Chase is a life regent of the University of Hartford and an honorary trustee of its Hartt School. The family’s support included a pledge benefiting university operations, Hartt scholarships and Hillel, recognised in the naming of Chase Family Arena.",
